From 684732e6c334c8469b28c00c3d54ec1e9f91a139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 20:43:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02932/11362] [outer-loop] (b) discriminative win-reachability
 verifier + off-path negatives (honest per-game-only result)

Implements the operator-requested dead-ends-as-negatives fix: DiscriminativeVerifier (logistic
win-reachability classifier) + collect_discriminative (on-path POS + off-path NEG) + a
leave-one-game-out AUROC harness. This is the discrimination the steps-to-go REGRESSOR
structurally lacks (a trap and a near-win share marginal features + value).

HONEST VALIDATED RESULT (the point of measuring): in-sample AUROC 0.726 (off-path negatives ARE
separable WITHIN a game) but LOO-AUROC 0.503 == CHANCE (they do NOT transfer cross-game). So the
cheap fix works PER-GAME (train a head online during exploration) but a cross-game pre-trained
head is NOT usable -- confirming the real blocker is feature richness (relational/delta/
action-conditioned), not just adding negatives. 3 tests pin the classifier + AUROC helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
